WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.656
WHERE and HAVING both filter but they operate at
different stages WHERE

00:00:05.682 --> 00:00:11.317
filters individual source rows before grouping
happens For example keeping only

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:15.066
sales where price is at least twenty-five dollars
removes rows before the

00:00:15.093 --> 00:00:20.979
category totals are calculated HAVING filters
completed groups after

00:00:21.006 --> 00:00:26.758
aggregation For example keeping categories whose
total quantity is greater than ten

00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:32.112
requires the grouped total to exist first A simple
test is to

00:00:32.125 --> 00:00:35.480
ask whether the condition refers to an individual
row or to a

00:00:35.494 --> 00:00:41.179
group measure If it is a row condition think WHERE
If

00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:45.284
it is a condition on COUNT SUM AVG or another
grouped measure

00:00:45.442 --> 00:00:51.000
think HAVING Keeping these roles separate makes
aggregation queries much

00:00:51.026 --> 00:00:52.302
easier to reason about
